Notebook[{Cell["Rotating third-vector obstruction and tied-profile rank certificate", 
   "Title"], Cell["Exact full-chain residuals and a no-go test for constant \
sector reweighting", "Subtitle"], Cell["Purpose and boundary", "Section"], 
  Cell["This notebook combines the exact rotating three-form residual with \
the exact polynomial rank certificates.  It proves that the tested constant \
reweighting ansatz cannot preserve the static anchor and close the rotating \
chain once every repeated Eq. (3.31) primitive profile is tied consistently.  \
It does not prove where the missing tensor structure first enters, and it \
does not localize the mismatch uniquely to raw hGeom.", "Text"], 
  Cell["Physical interpretation", "Section"], Cell["Allowing twelve raw \
occurrences to vary independently gives a twelve-dimensional solution space, \
but that freedom is nonphysical: one primitive profile cannot carry different \
coefficients in the metric, scalar, and vector descendants.  Enforcing the \
four profile inheritance relations makes the exact system inconsistent.  The \
predual-scalar rows are an intentionally wrong-stage negative control; the \
physical scalar repair belongs to the second postdual map and leaves the third-vector \
obstruction unchanged.", "Text"], Cell["Convention bridge", "Section"], 
  Cell["The flat-index symbol convention is epsilonLower[0,1,2,3,4]=+1, epsilonUpper[0,1,2,3,4]=-1 and the physical potential is A3=+Hzero^(-1) Theta. The curved tensor is the five-vielbein transform of that symbol. Because the notebook chart reverses the physical orientation, its curved lower component is epsilonLower[t,r,theta,phi,psi]=-Sqrt[-g]. The final +C wedge (d h+F wedge G) multiplier therefore requires h=-Exp[2 Phi] star5 F3+(alphaPrime/8) J. Relative to the archived component implementation, both the curved-lower-tensor sign and the Hodge-duality sign reverse, leaving the actual J contraction and the embedded rational residuals unchanged. Notebook 23 supplies the direct ten-component recalculation; the static guard below records the same convention locally.", "Text"], Cell["Self-contained exact calculation", 
   "Section"], Cell[BoxData["(* Self-contained rotating C3 obstruction and \
exact-rank certificate.\n   All rational residuals and coefficient matrices \
are embedded below.\n   No cache, script, notebook, or fitted target \
potential is imported. *)\n\nClearAll[\"Global`*\"];\n$HistoryLength = \
0;\nframeEpsilonLowerOrdered = 1; frameEpsilonUpperOrdered = -1;\ncoordinateLowerEpsilonSign = -1; positiveThirdPotentialSign = 1;\nstaticStarF3Component = -qzero Sin[theta]/4;\nstaticHorizontalHComponent = qzero Sin[theta]/4;\nconventionLedger = <|\n  \"FrameEpsilonConvention\" -> TrueQ[{frameEpsilonLowerOrdered,frameEpsilonUpperOrdered} === {1,-1}],\n  \"OrientationReversingChart\" -> TrueQ[coordinateLowerEpsilonSign == -1],\n  \"PositiveEq41ThirdPotential\" -> TrueQ[positiveThirdPotentialSign == 1],\n  \"FinalActionMinusDualityStatic\" -> TrueQ[FullSimplify[staticHorizontalHComponent + staticStarF3Component == 0]]|>;\ntripleOrder = {{1,2,3},{1,2,4},{1,2,5},{1,3,4},{1,3,5},\n  \
{1,4,5},{2,3,4},{2,3,5},{2,4,5},{3,4,5}};\nfullChainResidualAtR2 = {0, 0, \
-38054/47544651, 61340/30255687,\n  0, 0, 0, 0, 0, \
-22478/30255687};\nfullChainClosureResidualAtR2 = \
46775306/5752902771;\nnonzeroResidualTriples = Pick[tripleOrder,\n  \
Not[PossibleZeroQ[#]] & /@ fullChainResidualAtR2];\nresidualLedger = <|\n  \
\"FullChainClosureObstructionNonzero\" ->\n    \
Not[PossibleZeroQ[fullChainClosureResidualAtR2]],\n  \
\"OnlyExpectedResidualTriples\" ->\n    nonzeroResidualTriples === \
{{1,2,5},{1,3,4},{3,4,5}}|>;\nstageAnnotations = <|\n  \
\"StaticTorsionFreeHAnchor\" -> \"PASS in the independently rerun inverse-h \
regression\",\n  \"RotatingTorsionFreeHAnchor\" -> \"FAIL in the \
independently rerun inverse-h regression\",\n  \"ScalarStage\" -> \"the \
corrected scalar term is postdual and leaves the predual h input \
unchanged\"|>;\n\n(* Exact matrices from the polynomially canonicalized joint \
system.\n   Each pair is {coefficient matrix, right-hand side}.  Variable \
order is\n   stated below and follows the action/map sectors, fine sectors, \
then raw\n   Eq. (3.31) profile sectors. *)\nrankData = {{{{0, -154350, 0, \
